<#@ template language="C#" #>
<#@ parameter name="Database" type="CodeGenNew.Core.DatabaseModel" #>
<#@ parameter name="Project" type="CodeGenNew.Core.ProjectSettings" #>
<#@ import namespace="CodeGenNew.Core" #>
<#
    // ==========================================================================================
    // RS_TestApprovals_v1.tt
    // Generates: tests/api/approval_routes.rs   (whole-database; the output folder is the Rust crate's folder)
    // Integration tests of the routes RS_Approvals writes for RowApprovals, run in process over a scratch database like RS_Test. Before each test the people of the user table (a requester and two
    // approvers, with ApproverTable also a person approved for another table only) and a row of the first RowApprovals table are added with plain SQL, and they are removed after it; the keys are fixed
    // numbers far above the usual ones. The cases: a person the user table does not know, a row that is not there, a request and a second one while it waits, a person who may not decide, the list of
    // waiting requests, withdrawal by the requester only, the four eyes, a decision written once and the history of every cycle. The words are ApprovalWords, as in the other stacks' tests.
    // Written only for a project with RustTests=true, ApiAuth and RowApprovals when the user table and the table can be filled from the schema (a column that cannot be NULL needs an example value).
    // Needs Client.start_signed_out, Client.as_person and Client.pool of tests/api/test_support.rs (RS_EssentialTests); an older copy of that file is refreshed by running essentials with the replace option.
    // Full notes: Docs/TemplateNotes/RS_Test_v1.md
    // ==========================================================================================
    if (RustApprovalTests.Applies(Database, Project))
    {
        Write("@@@FILE tests/api/approval_routes.rs@@@\n" + RustApprovalTests.File(Database, Project));
    }
#>
